==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AccessControl  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AccessControl.als
    rationale: F_AccessControl is the load-bearing constraint tying (relationship, opKind) to the permission matrix. Clearing it removes the link; the injection forces an explicit sharee-doing-DELETE success, which the matrix forbids — so LeastPrivilege and the related FRs must produce a counterexample.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_011_ShareeCannotDelete, FR_010_OwnerOnlySharesChange
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_ShareeCannotDelete: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_010_OwnerOnlySharesChange: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact lets two AuditEntries describe the same logical operation event (a rewrite/duplicate), which is exactly what append-only forbids. The injection forces two such entries to coexist.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_017_AuditAppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_017_AuditAppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditOnePerMutation  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AuditOnePerMutation.als
    rationale: Clearing this removes the requirement that every successful mutating operation be backed by an audit entry; the injection constructs an orphan state change — a successful PATCH with no matching AuditEntry — which violates the per-event audit invariant.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_015_PerEventAudit, FR_018_NoOrphanStateChange
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_PerEventAudit: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_NoOrphanStateChange: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAttribution  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AuditAttribution.als
    rationale: Clearing this lets an AuditEntry record an actor that is not the operation's caller, i.e., misattribution. The injection forces a recordedActor mismatch.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_016_AuditFields
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditFields: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_SharedWithSameTeam  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_SharedWithSameTeam.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets a sharee live in a different team than the task — exactly the cross-team-sharing escape FR-012 prohibits. The injection makes such a configuration exist.
    expected to FAIL: FR_012_NoCrossTeamSharing
      - FR_012_NoCrossTeamSharing: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_UnauthenticatedRejected  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_UnauthenticatedRejected.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the gate forcing successful operations to be authenticated. The injection produces a successful unauthenticated operation, breaking the auth invariant.
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere, FR_001_AuthRequired
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: FAIL (expected)

